{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he saw the first portion for himself.</b> Even though the children of Ammon and Moab contest it, as we find in the case of Yiftach. And the reason: <b>for there the portion of the lawgiver is hidden</b>, as Rashi explained. Another interpretation: <b>for there the portion of the lawgiver</b> etc. — for there is the inheritance and portion of Reuben, who is called lawgiver, as it is written: ״בִּפְלֻגּוֹת רְאוּבֵן גְּדֹלִים חִקְקֵי־לֵב״ (in the divisions of Reuben were great searchings of heart); there it is hidden and set in order already. Another interpretation: it also refers to Gad, and calls him by the name of his greatness and importance — <b>lawgiver</b>, a prince and judge."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:31.455215261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}